# Agent Instructions — {{WORKSPACE_NAME|default("AI Workspace")}}

This workspace has **two purposes**, and this file governs both:

1. **Cross-repo AI context** — it coordinates changes across sibling repositories so AI agents and developers can reason about and modify the entire system in a single unified session.
2. **Project / Delivery planning** — it hosts a durable planning tree under `docs/planning/` that agents help author, sequence, refine, and keep synchronized with implementation reality.

Read this file before making any changes.

Also read `docs/architecture.md` (cross-repo component boundaries), `docs/workflow.md` (conventions & DoR/DoD), and `docs/planning/README.md` (active cycles/increments) before planning or suggesting architectural changes.

---

## Instruction Precedence & Reading Path

Use this order when workspace documents overlap:

1. `AGENTS.md` routes work and defines workspace-wide safety and ownership boundaries.
2. `docs/workflow.md` is the canonical source for cross-cutting process rules, story sizing, and DoR/DoD gates.
3. `docs/architecture.md` is the canonical summary of current cross-repository state.
4. Accepted ADRs (`docs/adr/`) record binding architectural decisions; newer superseding ADRs win.
5. The [skill index](.github/skills/README.md) routes specialized tasks to task-specific `SKILL.md` procedures.
6. Planning files (timebox READMEs, goal/epic plans, and story files) define scope and acceptance criteria for specific work items.

